{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA convergence test that RE-DERIVES what the send path does — instead of DRIVING the send path\nand capturing what it produced — measures the helper it named, not the convergence it claims.\nIt stays green when the send path drifts, which is the only failure it exists to catch. This\nhappened twice in the same module:\n\n1. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py` modelled\n   the landed Jira body as `comment_limits.truncate_comment_body(emitted_body)`. When\n   `emersed-specific-mutt` moved the Cloud send path onto `AdfCodec.fit_outbound`, the model\n   went stale and the test kept passing while live convergence was broken (bug\n   `abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey`, 836 unmarked duplicate comments in live Jira).\n2. The first draft of that bug's own fix re-derived the send side as\n   `fit_preserving_marker(_decorate_outbound_comment(body), codec.fit_outbound)` — a copy of\n   the composition under test — and passed Gerrit CI with `Verified +1`. Seeding the exact\n   original mistake back into `add_comment` left it GREEN (8 passed re-derived vs 2 failed\n   captured, recorded in this ticket's history).\n\nThe concrete test defect is already fixed: commit `103729e90c` landed\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py`, whose\n`_send` helper captures the `--body` argument from a real `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` call with\nonly `acli_subprocess._run_acli` stubbed. What remains is guardrail work: nothing in the repo\ntells the next test author which of the two shapes is correct — `make lint`, the complexity\nratchet and code review all passed the re-derived version.\n\n## Approach\n\nRecord the rule in the shared test-design standard — the guidance test authors are already\ndirected to at oracle-design time (`examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md:627` and\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md:214` both point at `test-design.md` in their\nskill directory) — rather than inventing a new document. Add a titled paragraph to\n`examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` §4 \"Trigger the mechanism; assert the contract\"\n(the section that governs what an oracle may assert, and one of the sections that \"apply to\nevery test\" per the scale-ceremony rule, so no section renumbering is needed): in a\nconvergence/agreement test, the side of the assertion that represents an external effect must\nbe CAPTURED from the real call site — drive the production entry point with only the\nirreducible boundary stubbed and capture what it handed the boundary — never RE-DERIVED by\nrecomposing the helpers that call site uses today. Use the two instances above as the compact\nworked example (stale re-derived model vs. the landed captured `--body` oracle). Then sync the\nbyte-identical per-skill copies exactly per `examples/agent-skills/README.md` §\"The shared\ntest-design standard\" (`cp` canonical over `rebar-debug`/`rebar-implement`/`rebar-brainstorm`\ncopies); the existing gating test `tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py` enforces the sync.\n\nFor the mechanical-check AC, evaluate the proposed lint (flag a test that imports the same\nfit/encode helper the module under test uses on both sides of an equality assertion) against\nthe current tree and record the verdict as a comment on this ticket. Default decision: do NOT\nadd it — 17 test files under `tests/` already import\n`fit_outbound`/`truncate_comment_body`/`fit_preserving_marker`, and the legitimate\ncharacterization shape (e.g. `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py`\ndeliberately pins `fit_comment` equal to the send-path fit by calling both helpers) is\nsyntactically identical to the defective shape; whether one assertion side \"represents an\nexternal effect\" is intent, not syntax, so the check cannot be written without flagging the\nsanctioned tests. The comment records the survey numbers so the decision is auditable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` — add the capture-don't-re-derive rule +\n  worked example to §4 (canonical copy).\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/test-design.md` — byte-identical sync of the canonical.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/test-design.md` — byte-identical sync.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/test-design.md` — byte-identical sync.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only change — no new testable runtime behavior. The one existing gating test\nthat covers this edit is the copy-sync guard: `pytest tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py`\nmust pass (it fails if any per-skill copy diverges from the canonical file). `make lint` and\n`make typecheck` run as usual.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` §4 states the rule — the external-effect\n      side of a convergence assertion is captured from the real call site, not recomputed\n      from the helpers that call site uses — and names both worked examples from this ticket\n      (the stale `truncate_comment_body` model and the captured `--body` oracle that replaced\n      it). Check: `grep -n \"re-derive\" examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md` hits\n      inside §4 and a read of the paragraph confirms both examples.\n- [ ] All three consuming skill copies are byte-identical to the canonical file. Check:\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py` passes.\n- [ ] The mechanical-check evaluation is recorded as a comment on this ticket: the decision\n      (add / don't add) plus the false-positive evidence (the survey counts of legitimate\n      tests importing the shared fit helpers). Check: `rebar show` on this ticket shows the\n      comment."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787366965830595001,"uuid":"78a54336-9135-49e9-af4d-501a67cd5542"}